  2 | // Spec: .agent-runs/snowy-neon-noon-revision/specs/02-noon-staging.md (contract 00).
  3 | //
  4 | // Pure and deterministic: same arguments -> same result. No DOM, no imports,
  5 | // no mutable state. noonStage() returns render-ready fields; the renderer
  6 | // passes {model:'noon', x, y, scale, facing, pose, uid} plus the returned t
  7 | // straight to renderCharacter().
  8 | //
  9 | // ---------------------------------------------------------------- walk math
 10 | // The Noon rig (models/noon/original-actor.js) plants a foot for the first
 11 | // ST=0.55 of each 0.72 s walk cycle; the planted foot's local x sweeps
 12 | // +46 -> -46 (92 local units in 0.396 s = 232.32 local u/s). With
 13 | // worldX = anchor.x + footLocalX*scale*facing, a planted foot stays fixed in
 14 | // world x iff d(anchor.x)/dt = 232.32*scale px/s along +x (facing=1).
 15 | //
 16 | // The walk-in path runs anchor.x 533 -> 690 while scale grows 0.47 -> 0.5
 17 | // (perspective). With s(x) linear, dx/dt = V*s(x) integrates in closed form:
 18 | //   s(t)      = 0.47 * exp(0.03*V*tau/157)
 19 | //   x(tau)    = 533 + (157/0.03)*0.47*(exp(0.03*V*tau/157) - 1)
 20 | //   WALK_T    = (157/(0.03*V)) * ln(0.5/0.47)  ≈ 1.394 s of walking
 21 | // The rig clock advances 1:1 with shot-local time, offset by WALK_RIG_T0 so
 22 | // the walk phase lands on a good plant phase (~w=0.88) exactly at WALK_T,
 23 | // minimising the walk->idle foot pop (same trade-off as 60s scene02).
 24 | //
 25 | // Feet y: the floor recedes from y1185 (rear threshold) to y1245 (counter
 26 | // back). A single anchor.y cannot put BOTH feet on the floor while they are
 27 | // ~20 world px apart in x, so anchor.y tracks floorY() under a support point
 28 | // xEff = support-weighted mean of the planted feet's world x (weights ramp
 29 | // in/out over the first/last 0.06 of each stance). During a pure single-
 30 | // stance phase xEff equals that foot's fixed world x, so its sole sits at
 31 | // floorY(footX) with zero drift on both axes; only during the ~70 ms
 32 | // double-support hand-offs does the trailing sole ease by a few px — reads
 33 | // as weight transfer, not sliding. Reported feet[] use the identical math,
 34 | // so contact shadows land on the drawn soles.
