  2 | // for Snowy Neon. Shot `rear-entry` (film 5.72–8.40 s, local 0..2.68) is a
  3 | // full-frame interior angle on the rear doorway: Noon walks out of the dark
  4 | // void carrying the empty copper coin tray and settles at the counter side.
  5 | //
  6 | //   rearEntrySvg({ local, duration = 2.68, seconds }) -> complete
  7 | //   <svg viewBox="0 0 1080 1920">…</svg> string. Pure/deterministic: same
  8 | //   arguments -> same markup. No DOM, no Math.random, no wall clock.
  9 | //
 10 | // Walk / foot-slide derivation (the 60s scene02 keys do NOT guarantee this):
 11 | //   The Noon rig's footAt() plants a stance foot for ST=0.55 of the 0.72 s
 12 | //   cycle, travelling 2*S=92 local units in 0.396 s  =>  ground speed
 13 | //   92/0.396 = 232.323 local px/s; at scale s the world speed must equal
 14 | //   232.323·s px/s along the facing direction or the planted foot slides.
 15 | //   Here scale is held at SCALE=0.6 for the whole shot, so while pose==='walk'
 16 | //   her head anchor advances at SPEED = 92/(0.72·0.55)·0.6 = 139.394 px/s in
 17 | //   +x (facing=1). A planted foot's world x = bodyX + footLocalX·scale then
 18 | //   stays fixed to <0.1 px (the stance foot retreats at exactly SPEED in
 19 | //   local·scale units). Feet y is likewise held constant (FEET_Y=1310) during
 20 | //   the walk so the sole never drifts vertically inside a stance.
 21 | //   The walk phase is seeded at w0=0.877 of the cycle (rig t0 = w0·0.72 =
 22 | //   0.63144) so the left foot is planted on the idle stance (-17 local) when
 23 | //   she steps off; rig t = t0 + (local - WALK_START) while walking.
 24 | //   Walk window local 0.45–1.90 s covers 515 -> ~717 px (≈3.5 gait cycles,
 25 | //   a short read of steps at this scale); pose 'idle' before and for the last
 26 | //   ≈0.8 s after, matching "settles near the counter side".
 27 | //
 28 | // Layer order (binding, see REAR_ENTRY_LAYERS): back wall z0 and rear door z1
 29 | // are the lowest groups; floor/walls z10; props z20–40; Noon z50; counter
